      "path": "index.html",
      "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Pixel Math Quiz</title>\n  <style>\n    :root {\n      --bg: #1a1a2e;\n      --card: #16213e;\n      --text: #e0e0e0;\n      --accent: #e94560;\n      --accent-hover: #ff6b81;\n      --border: #0f3460;\n    }\n    * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      min-height: 100vh;\n      display: flex;\n      justify-content: center;\n      align-items: center;\n      background: var(--bg);\n      font-family: 'Courier New', monospace;\n      font-size: 18px;\n      color: var(--text);\n      padding: 16px;\n    }\n    .card {\n      background: var(--card);\n      border: 4px solid var(--border);\n      border-radius: 8px;\n      padding: 24px 20px;\n      width: 100%;\n      max-width: 400px;\n      text-align: center;\n      box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px #0a0a1a;\n    }\n    h1 {\n      font-size: 1.4rem;\n      margin: 0 0 16px;\n      letter-spacing: 2px;\n      text-transform: uppercase;\n      color: var(--accent);\n    }\n    #question {\n      font-size: 2rem;\n      font-weight: bold;\n      margin: 16px 0 24px;\n      min-height: 2.5rem;\n      word-break: break-word;\n    }\n    .answers {\n      display: flex;\n      gap: 12px;\n      justify-content: center;\n      flex-wrap: wrap;\n      margin-bottom: 20px;\n    }\n    button {\n      font-family: inherit;\n      font-size: 1.2rem;\n      padding: 12px 24px;\n      border: 3px solid var(--border);\n      border-radius: 6px;\n      background: var(--accent);\n      color: #fff;\n      cursor: pointer;\n      transition: background 0.15s, transform 0.1s;\n      min-width: 80px;\n    }\n    button:hover:not(:disabled) { background: var(--accent-hover); }\n    button:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #fff; outline-offset: 3px; }\n    button:active:not(:disabled) { transform: scale(0.96); }\n    button:disabled { opacity: 0.6; cursor: not-allowed; }\n    #score {\n      font-size: 1.2rem;\n      margin: 12px 0;\n      color: var(--accent);\n    }\n    .controls { display: flex; gap: 12px; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }\n    #next { background: #0f3460; }\n    #next:hover:not(:disabled) { background: #1a4a7a; }\n    #restart { background: #533483; }\n    #restart:hover:not(:disabled) { background: #6b4a9e; }\n    .label { font-size: 0.9rem; opacity: 0.8; }\n    [hidden] { display: none !important; }\n    @media (max-width: 400px) {\n      body { font-size: 16px; }\n      #question { font-size: 1.6rem; }\n      button { font-size: 1rem; padding: 10px 18px; }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"card\">\n    <h1>Pixel Math Quiz</h1>\n    <p id=\"question\">2 + 2 = ?</p>\n    <div class=\"answers\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Answer choices\">\n      <button id=\"answer-a\" aria-label=\"Answer A\">4</button>\n      <button id=\"answer-b\" aria-label=\"Answer B\">5</button>\n    </div>\n    <p id=\"score\">Score: 0</p>\n    <div class=\"controls\">\n      <button id=\"next\" disabled>Next</button>\n      <button id=\"restart\">Restart</button>\n    </div>\n  </main>\n  <script>\n    (function() {\n      const questionEl = document.getElementById('question');\n      const answerA = document.getElementById('answer-a');\n      const answerB = document.getElementById('answer-b');\n      const scoreEl = document.getElementById('score');\n      const nextBtn = document.getElementById('next');\n      const restartBtn = document.getElementById('restart');\n\n      const questions = [\n        { text: '2 + 2 = ?', a: '4', b: '5', correct: 'a' },\n        { text: '3 + 3 = ?', a: '5', b: '6', correct: 'b' }\n      ];\n\n      let current = 0;\n      let score = 0;\n      let answered = false;\n\n      function render() {\n        const q = questions[current];\n        questionEl.textContent = q ? q.text : 'Finished';\n        answerA.textContent = q ? q.a : '';\n        answerB.textContent = q ? q.b : '';\n        answerA.disabled = !q || answered;\n        answerB.disabled = !q || answered;\n        nextBtn.disabled = !answered || !q;\n        scoreEl.textContent = 'Score: ' + score;\n      }\n\n      function handleAnswer(choice) {\n        if (answered || !questions[current]) return;\n        answered = true;\n        if (choice === questions[current].correct) {\n          score += 1;\n        }\n        render();\n      }\n\n      answerA.addEventListener('click', function() { handleAnswer('a'); });\n      answerB.addEventListener('click', function() { handleAnswer('b'); });\n\n      nextBtn.addEventListener('click', function() {\n        if (!answered) return;\n        if (current < questions.length - 1) {\n          current += 1;\n          answered = false;\n          render();\n        } else {\n          current = questions.length;\n          answered = false;\n          render();\n        }\n      });\n\n      restartBtn.addEventListener('click', function() {\n        current = 0;\n        score = 0;\n        answered = false;\n        render();\n      });\n\n      render();\n    })();\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>",
      "description": ""
    },
    {
      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Math Quiz\n\nAn offline, pixel-style two-question math quiz built with HTML, CSS, and plain JavaScript. No packages, storage, or network requests.\n\n## How to Run\n\nOpen `index.html` in any modern browser. No server required.\n\n## Features\n\n- Two questions: `2 + 2 = ?` and `3 + 3 = ?`\n- Answer choices lock after selection\n- Score increments only for correct answers\n- `Next` button advances questions; after the second question, shows `Finished`\n- `Restart` resets to the first question and score 0\n- Keyboard accessible with visible focus, hover, and pressed states\n- Responsive down to 360px wide\n\n## Controls\n\n- **Answer A / Answer B**: Select an answer (locks after one click)\n- **Next**: Go to the next question (enabled after answering)\n- **Restart**: Reset the quiz\n\n## Accessibility\n\n- Buttons have `aria-label` attributes\n- Focus outlines are visible\n- All interactive elements are keyboard reachable\n\n## File Structure\n\n- `index.html` — contains all HTML, CSS, and JavaScript (under 230 lines)\n",
      "description": ""
    }
  ]
